import Mathlib.FieldTheory.Galois.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Trace.Basic

/-!
# Additive Hilbert 90 for a cyclic Galois extension

Let `L / K` be a Galois extension whose Galois group is generated by `σ`. Then the kernel of
the field trace `Tr_{L/K}` is the image of `σ - 1`:

`ker (Tr_{L/K}) = range (σ - 1)`.

This is Theorem 24.1(i) of MIT 18.785 (Number Theory I), Lecture 24. Mathlib proves trace
surjectivity and multiplicative Hilbert 90 in `Mathlib.FieldTheory.Galois.Hilbert90`, where
additive Hilbert 90 is listed as future work; this module fills that gap for cyclic Galois
groups, without any group-cohomology packaging.

## Proof outline

The inclusion `range (σ - 1) ≤ ker Tr` follows from trace invariance under automorphisms.
Both sides then have complementary finrank: `ker (σ - 1)` is the base field (an element
fixed by `σ` is fixed by every automorphism, hence lies in `K` for a Galois extension), so
it has `K`-finrank one; `range Tr` is all of `K` by trace surjectivity, so it also has
`K`-finrank one. Rank-nullity applied to both maps then forces the inclusion to be an
equality.
-/

variable {K L : Type*} [Field K] [Field L] [Algebra K L] [FiniteDimensional K L]
  [IsGalois K L]

namespace Algebra
end Algebra
